all cultures around the world have told  stories about spooky creatures or forces  that try to explain some of the  mysterious and unexplained aspects of  our world creatures and stories that  often have a function to be educational  and to keep people especially children  from wandering about in strange places  or at night and which will inevitably be  exploited in some crappy Hollywood movie  at some point  in Sweden and the Nordic countries we  have a bunch of these stories and  creatures and one of the most spooky and  scary ones is the creature known as the  mare a ghostly figure that creeps up on  you when you sleep and which most  probably is meant to represent the what  we know today as the dreaded experience  of sleep paralysis  so join me for the first episode of this  year's shocktober as we talk about the  mayor  [Music]  [Music]  the mayor is a creature that has existed  in the folklore of Sweden and its  surrounding countries for a long time  there are even mentions of the mayor in  snory's Ada or the prose Ada written in  the 12th century these stories are of  course probably taken from even older  material and it's likely that the mayor  is a figure that has been around since a  while before the 13th century at least  in Sweden the mayor is called Maran and  she has similar names in surrounding  countries she could be referred to by  many other names as well but modern or  the mayor is the name that seems to have  stuck across history  the etymology of the word Mata is  thought to have originally meant  something like crushing or oppression  which will make sense when we describe  her features but significantly it is  from the mayor that we get the word  nightmare for when we have a bad dream  this connection is present in Swedish as  well where the name for nightmare is  more dram meaning literally mer dream  and indeed the mayor is primarily  associated with sleep and the bedroom  while she can take on many different  forms all stories about the mayor share  the idea that she will somehow creep  into your house at night approach your  bed while you are sleeping and  essentially sit on your chest pretty  creepy stuff as I said the mayor could  take on many different forms usually she  is considered of as a human woman  sometimes dressed in black but many  other times she also takes the form of a  cat a dog or an owl the function was the  same though as it would always show up  in your bedroom and usually sit on your  chest which create a kind of oppressing  kind of a hard feeling of having a hard  time breathing basically there have been  some ideas floating around regarding the  origins or nature of the mare some say a  mer was a woman that had been cursed  somehow that she lived a normal life  during the day but at night would turn  into a frightening creature that invaded  people's homes  other stories relate that she was rather  just an evil person that made a  conscious decision to terrorize people  and it wasn't just people that had to  withstand attacks from the mayor even  animals could fall victim he was often  believed that if the horses on a farm  for example appeared tired and sweaty in  the morning for no apparent reason this  meant that they had been visited by the  mayor during the night the horses would  also sometimes have small braids in  their Mane which would be called mod  flat or mare braids now obviously there  are also sometimes certain erotic  aspects to this Legend some stories say  that the mayor was primarily driven by  jealousy and a desire to be close to men  particularly in southern Sweden there  was a widespread belief that a mayor was  in fact the spirit of an unmarried dead  woman there are even stories about  people who married a mayor there is a  story about a person a guy who is  visited by this creature and then  basically blocks off all exits to the  house so she so he traps the mare in his  house basically and then forces her to  to marry him essentially not that I  recommend anyone to do this but that is  one such story in any case stories about  visitations from the mayor are usually  pretty similar she will enter your  bedroom and sit on your chest  people experience that they have trouble  breathing because of the huge pressure  on their chest as well as the sensation  of being paralyzed so not being able to  move now obviously this can be pretty  safely connected to a known condition  today that we call sleep paralysis  many people myself included have  experienced waking up in the middle of  the night unable to move many also  experienced that pressure on the chest  that is often described in the stories  and some also experience hallucinations  of actually seeing figures standing over  you or sitting on your chest as a result  of the brain not quite having broken up  yet it could be a truly terrifying  experience especially if you're not used  to it and indeed for those of us who  have experienced sleep paralysis you  could say that we have been visited by  the mayor because it's clear that the  stories about the mayor is a way to  explain or or to personify this rather  common condition that people have  experienced historically and still  experience today right it's a way to  sort of explain this condition by  pointing to a a supernatural creature  that somehow personifies it and not just  sleep paralysis but basically any bad  dream was seen as being caused by the  Mare and that is why it's called a  nightmare so any bad dream is the mayor  that is visiting you and causing this  bad dream and that should make you look  twice across the room the next time you  wake up in the middle of the night  possibly because these experiences and  conditions such as sleep paralysis are  so common there are many stories and  accounts from around the Nordic  countries of people encountering a mare  in one account from 1873 in eastern  Sweden a woman tells us quote back home  in Husby people believe the mayor was a  living person that was jealous  than the jealous person could visit the  one she wanted to hurt there was an old  lady close to where I lived in Husby who  complained to my mother that the mayor  was terrorizing her at night that she  would come floating in through the  chamber door even though it was locked  she would recognize her as one of her  neighbors who would then lie on her  chest so she couldn't breathe  in another account from 1864 quote the  mayor would bother both humans and  animals it was a spirit that comes over  you when you sleep it lies across your  chest and it feels like something hairy  just a few years ago I myself was  looking through the archives in a local  Museum here in Stockholm and I came  across an old report from a village or  region in Western Sweden a small village  where we usually spend our summers and  I'm probably grown up there and so on  and this was a report from like early  last century that basically said that  multiple people had spotted the mayor in  that Village which you know might have  felt better if I didn't see that before  going that summer anyway the mayor shows  up all across this region of Europe and  appears quite common it's a pretty  creepy creature that most people would  want to keep away so how does one  protect oneself from the mayor well  there are several traditions and stories  about this too depending on what region  you are in ETC obviously in Christian  times you could do things like hang up  crucifix over your bed or keep a copy of  the Bible or a song book under your  pillow or next to the bed so aside from  this you should avoid going to bed on a  full stomach you could put horseshoes  under your bed or sing protective songs  that often tell the mayor to count  various things before attacking you see  it was believed that she was really bad  at math and giving her a task to for  example count all the trees in the  forest first meant that she wouldn't  have time to attack before morning  arrived some traditions also state that  you can cure a mare now this only works  in those cases where the mayor was  thought to be a living cursed human  being of course but since the person in  question didn't know that she was a  mayor during the night you could tell  her often in the moment when she returns  to her body so when the marriage out  during the night haunting people in  their sleep eventually in the morning  the mayor will return to her home to her  regular sort of body and Consciousness  and if you tell the mayor at the very  moment where she sort of reunites with  her body that should for some reason  cure her and she will return to just  being her normal self as you can tell  and as is usually the case with things  like this in terms of folklore and  mythology and religion there are there's  a diversity of stories and ideas about  the mayor depending on which region you  are in there are different conceptions  of what the mayor looked like what her  function was and of course also across  time things and these stories will will  change inevitably but there are a few  things that always remain  associated with the mayor for one thing  that she is really creepy but also  certain other characteristics like  visiting you at night in your bedroom  and sitting on your chest the fact that  we can kind of confirm that most or at  least many of these stories are real  because they are most likely based on  the common and real experience of sleep  paralysis makes it all the more  fascinating and kind of also all the  more spooky and creepy and I definitely  don't look forward to any possible  future episode of sleep paralysis if  there's any possibility that I will run  into this really scary creature but with  that said this is of course another  perfect fit for our yearly shocktober  Series where we discuss the darker and  spookier aspects of religion mythology  folklore and history I hope you are  properly spooked now although not too  much of course and that you are looking  forward 